        en: "committed step",
        cn: "定向步骤（committed step）",
        def_en: "The step past which the material has no destination other than this pathway's product. It is a statement about the SHAPE of the metabolic map, not about speed: it is not the same claim as rate-limiting (the slowest step, which sets throughput). Aspartate transcarbamoylase catalyses the first committed step of pyrimidine synthesis; glutamine-PRPP amidotransferase catalyses the first committed step of purine synthesis. Committed steps are the usual place to put regulation, which is why the two often coincide.",
        def_cn: "过了这一步，物料就再没有本路径产物以外的去处。这是一个关于**代谢图形状**的陈述，**不是关于速度**的：它**与「限速步骤」（最慢的那一步，决定通量）不是同一个断言**。天冬氨酸转氨甲酰酶催化嘧啶合成的第一个定向步骤；谷氨酰胺-PRPP 酰胺转移酶催化嘌呤合成的第一个定向步骤。定向步骤是安放调控的常见位置，这也是两者常常重合的原因。"
